  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather through next Thursday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nLow pressure continues to exit to the east, with a ridge of high\npressure slowly building in from the west. The center of high\npressure will remain south of our area into the weekend,\nmaintaining a light wind with westerly component; northwest in\non Saturday and southwest on Sunday.\n\nA prolonged period of dry weather continue through the weekend\nwith the next cold front moving through during the mid to late\nday Monday. Front will likely be as moisture-starved as the \nprevious FROPA. Temps following fropa will be chilly on Tuesday \nand Wednesday as Canadian high pressure builds in. The prolonged\ndry spell is very likely to persist through at least Thursday \nof next week.",
